\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Heal us, Emmanuel: hear our prayer;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 We wait to feel Thy rouch:
\par Deep-wounded souls to Thee repair;
\par And, Saviour, we are such.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our faith is feeble, we confess;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 We faintly trust Thy word:
\par But wilt Thou pity us the less?
\par Be that far from Thee, Lord.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Remember him who once applied
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With trembling for relief;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Lord, I believe! with tears he cried,
\par O help my unbelief!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   She, too, who touched Thee in the press,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 And healing virtue stole,
\par Was answered: Daughter, go in peace,
\par  Thy faith hath made thee whole.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  Like her, with hopes and fears we come,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  To touch Thee, if we may:
\par  O send us not despairing home.
\par \pard      Send none unhealed away. Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

